WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:01.680
Matthew 11

00:01.680 --> 00:05.980
When Jesus had finished instructing his twelve disciples,

00:06.140 --> 00:09.000
he went on from there to teach and preach in their cities.

00:09.660 --> 00:12.880
Now when John heard in prison about the deeds of the Christ,

00:13.300 --> 00:16.160
he sent word by his disciples and said to him,

00:16.840 --> 00:19.740
Are you the one who is to come, or shall we look for another?

00:20.520 --> 00:21.960
And Jesus answered them,

00:22.680 --> 00:25.600
Go, and tell John what you hear and see.

00:26.080 --> 00:29.180
The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk.

00:29.180 --> 00:33.540
Look, lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up,

00:33.860 --> 00:36.840
and the poor have good news preached to them.

00:37.420 --> 00:40.720
And blessed is the one who is not offended by me.

00:41.160 --> 00:45.780
As they went away, Jesus began to speak to the crowds concerning John.

00:46.200 --> 00:49.140
What did you go out into the wilderness to see?

00:49.600 --> 00:51.500
A reed shaken by the wind.

00:52.140 --> 00:54.200
What then did you go out to see?

00:54.620 --> 00:56.460
A man dressed in soft clothing?

00:57.420 --> 00:58.060
Behold,

00:58.300 --> 00:59.160
those who were in the wilderness,

00:59.160 --> 01:01.340
those who wear soft clothing are in kings' houses.

01:02.120 --> 01:04.240
What then did you go out to see?

01:04.600 --> 01:05.300
A prophet?

01:06.060 --> 01:08.760
Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.

01:09.420 --> 01:11.340
This is he of whom it is written,

01:12.100 --> 01:15.880
Behold, I send my messenger before your face,

01:16.060 --> 01:18.580
who will prepare your way before you.

01:19.480 --> 01:20.840
Truly I say to you,

01:21.280 --> 01:22.780
among those born of women,

01:23.100 --> 01:25.940
there has arisen no one greater than John the Baptist.

01:26.360 --> 01:29.140
Yet the one who is least in the kingdom of heaven,

01:29.160 --> 01:30.740
is greater than he.

01:31.560 --> 01:34.120
From the days of John the Baptist until now,

01:34.600 --> 01:36.160
the kingdom of heaven has suffered violence,

01:37.140 --> 01:39.100
and the violent take it by force.

01:39.660 --> 01:43.120
For all the prophets in the law prophesied until John.

01:43.640 --> 01:45.900
And if you are willing to accept it,

01:46.420 --> 01:48.740
he is Elijah who is to come.

01:49.540 --> 01:51.500
He who has ears to hear,

01:51.940 --> 01:53.000
let him hear.

01:54.940 --> 01:57.160
But to what shall I compare this generation?

01:57.160 --> 01:57.800
To this generation.

01:59.160 --> 02:01.940
It is like children sitting in the marketplaces,

02:02.360 --> 02:04.060
and calling to their playmates.

02:04.600 --> 02:06.300
We played the flute for you,

02:06.560 --> 02:07.860
and you did not dance.

02:08.280 --> 02:10.860
We sing a dirge, and you did not mourn.

02:11.400 --> 02:13.860
For John came neither eating nor drinking,

02:14.240 --> 02:15.020
and they say,

02:15.460 --> 02:16.600
He has a demon.

02:17.420 --> 02:19.460
The Son of Man came eating and drinking,

02:19.580 --> 02:20.220
and they say,

02:20.720 --> 02:21.760
Look at him,

02:22.100 --> 02:23.940
a glutton and a drunkard,

02:23.940 --> 02:26.900
a friend of tax collectors and sinners.

02:28.440 --> 02:29.080
Yet,

02:29.160 --> 02:32.460
his wisdom is justified by her deeds.

02:33.460 --> 02:37.160
Then he began to denounce the cities where most of his mighty works had been done,

02:37.160 --> 02:39.160
because they did not repent.

02:39.160 --> 02:41.160
Woe to you, Chorazin!

02:41.160 --> 02:43.160
Woe to you, Bethsaida!

02:43.160 --> 02:49.160
For if the mighty works done in you had been done in Tyre and Sidon,

02:49.160 --> 02:54.160
they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.

02:54.160 --> 02:56.160
But I tell you,

02:56.160 --> 02:59.160
it will be more bearable on the day of judgment,

02:59.160 --> 03:01.160
for Tyre and Sidon,

03:01.160 --> 03:03.160
than for you.

03:03.160 --> 03:05.160
And you, Capernaum,

03:05.160 --> 03:07.160
will you be exalted to heaven?

03:07.160 --> 03:11.160
You will be brought down to Hades.

03:11.160 --> 03:13.160
For if the mighty works done in you

03:13.160 --> 03:15.160
had been done in Sodom,

03:15.160 --> 03:17.160
it would have remained until this day.

03:17.160 --> 03:19.160
But I tell you,

03:19.160 --> 03:21.160
that it will be more tolerable on the day of judgment

03:21.160 --> 03:23.160
for the land of Sodom,

03:23.160 --> 03:25.160
than for you.

03:25.160 --> 03:27.160
At that time Jesus declared,

03:27.160 --> 03:29.160
I thank you, Father,

03:29.160 --> 03:31.160
Lord of heaven and earth,

03:31.160 --> 03:33.160
that you have hidden these things

03:33.160 --> 03:35.160
from the wise and understanding,

03:35.160 --> 03:37.160
and revealed them to little children.

03:37.160 --> 03:39.160
Yes, Father,

03:39.160 --> 03:41.160
for such was your gracious will.

03:41.160 --> 03:43.160
All things have been handed over

03:43.160 --> 03:45.160
to me by my Father,

03:45.160 --> 03:47.160
and no one knows the Son except the Father,

03:47.160 --> 03:49.160
and no one knows the Father

03:49.160 --> 03:51.160
except the Son,

03:51.160 --> 03:53.160
and anyone to whom the Son

03:53.160 --> 03:55.160
chooses to reveal him.

03:55.160 --> 03:57.160
Come to me,

03:57.160 --> 03:59.160
all who labor

03:59.160 --> 04:01.160
and are heavy laden,

04:01.160 --> 04:03.160
and I will give you rest.

04:03.160 --> 04:05.160
Take my yoke upon you,

04:05.160 --> 04:07.160
and learn from me,

04:07.160 --> 04:09.160
for I am gentle and lowly in heart,

04:09.160 --> 04:11.160
and you will find rest

04:11.160 --> 04:13.160
for your souls.

04:13.160 --> 04:15.160
For my yoke is easy,

04:15.160 --> 04:17.160
and my burden is light.

